      "id": "R-background",
      "kind": "documented_requirement",
      "statement": "Unconsumed active shared work may finish after view departure; consumed work is abortable; canceled late fulfillment must not become new-attempt data.",
      "author": "execution_agent_source_review",
      "related": [],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "file": "inputs/README.md",
          "start": 12,
          "end": 16,
          "quote": "Multiple observers share one fetch. Unconsumed active work can finish into cache\nafter its view departs; consumed work is physically abortable. Cancellation\nreverts previous query data/status and settles the originating attempt. Late\nfulfillment cannot become a new attempt's data. Unknown unsubscribe is inert.\nThe component owns observer scope; the cache remains outside individual views."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "R-entry",
      "kind": "documented_requirement",
      "statement": "Initial entry and paused continuation differ in timing and eligibility; actual lazy reads record consumption.",
      "author": "execution_agent_source_review",
      "related": [],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "file": "inputs/README.md",
          "start": 6,
          "end": 11,
          "quote": "fetchStatus (idle/fetching/paused), and data. queryFn receives a lazy signal\naccessor. Each actual access records consumption; each fetch owns its controller\nand completion. Completion is asynchronous; initial online entry is synchronous,\npaused continuation resumes on a Promise turn. First start uses network mode;\ncontinuation also needs focus. 'always' can run offline; 'offlineFirst' allows\nfirst offline entry but retry can pause. Retries use explicit scheduler handles."
        }
      ]
    },
